265
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:24,916
double-sided tape
and some sort of luncheon meat.

266
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:31,798
Hey.

267
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,467
I've got a great idea.

268
00:10:33,508 --> 00:10:35,427
For party favors
for the shower.

269
00:10:35,469 --> 00:10:37,678
Okay, we get some
mahogany boxes

270
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,431
and carve everyone's
names in them

271
00:10:39,473 --> 00:10:41,182
and then inside
is each person's

272
00:10:41,224 --> 00:10:42,476
individual birthstone.

273
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:46,104
Okay.

274
00:10:46,146 --> 00:10:48,565
Okay.

275
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:50,150
All right,
you take care of that...

276
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:51,151
Okay.

277
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,902
And...

278
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:55,071
Meanwhile, the party is tomorrow

279
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:57,491
and we still
don't have a guest list.

280
00:10:57,532 --> 00:11:00,535
Okay, okay, well, okay, who
do we know that's coming?

281
00:11:00,577 --> 00:11:01,744
Me... Are you?

282
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:05,373
Hey.

283
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:07,584
Hey. What's up, Mon?

284
00:11:07,626 --> 00:11:09,252
I'm trying to make
something for Joey.

285
00:11:09,294 --> 00:11:10,378
Mind if I
raid your fridge?

286
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:12,422
Have at it.

287
00:11:12,464 --> 00:11:14,966
All right... turkey.

288
00:11:15,008 --> 00:11:17,093
That won't work.

289
00:11:17,135 --> 00:11:19,429
Cheese. That won't work.

290
00:11:19,471 --> 00:11:20,597
Olive loaf?!

291
00:11:20,639 --> 00:11:23,266
I hope that won't work.

292
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:27,770
Are you making him a sandwich?

293
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:31,483
No, it's more like a wrap.

294
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:34,693
Okay, so, uh...

295
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:36,112
I'm going to go, guys

296
00:11:36,154 --> 00:11:37,489
so you can get back to...

297
00:11:37,531 --> 00:11:39,824
deciding on what to get me
for a present.

298
00:11:43,161 --> 00:11:46,289
We have to get her a present?

299
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:47,790
Okay, but look.

300
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:50,210
♪ Look at what I got. ♪

301
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:52,546
It's her address book.

302
00:11:52,587 --> 00:11:54,839
We have a guest list. Ah.

303
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:56,424
Oh, my God, you're amazing.

304
00:11:56,466 --> 00:11:58,801
Did you just pull that
out of her purse?

305
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:02,556
Uh-huh. And, a little
seed money for the party.

306
00:12:02,597 --> 00:12:04,807
Oh, nice... Nice.

307
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:08,353
( loud knocking )

308
00:12:11,398 --> 00:12:13,400
Cassie?

309
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,402
Hey, Ross.

310
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:16,403
Hi.

311
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:18,863
It's been so long.

312
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:21,282
Last time I saw you

313
00:12:21,324 --> 00:12:23,493
you were setting up
your tent in line

314
00:12:23,535 --> 00:12:25,119
to see Return of the Jedi.

315
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:26,329
( stuttering )

316
00:12:26,371 --> 00:12:28,540
So you did see me that day

317
00:12:28,582 --> 00:12:31,376
because it seemed
like you didn't.

318
00:12:31,418 --> 00:12:32,711
( nervous laughter )

319
00:12:32,751 --> 00:12:34,421
Oh, yeah.
Sorry about that.

320
00:12:34,462 --> 00:12:36,256
It's okay.
Come on in.

321
00:12:36,297 --> 00:12:38,383
Thanks for letting
me stay here.

322
00:12:38,425 --> 00:12:40,427
I mean, Monica's place was nice

323
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:44,055
but her fiancé
sure stares a lot.

324
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:45,306
Ah...

325
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:52,439
BARRY WHITE:
♪ It feels so good ♪

326
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:56,443
♪ You lying here next to me. ♪

327
00:13:05,452 --> 00:13:06,703
Oh, my God.

328
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:09,581
You do a great Chandler.

329
00:13:11,291 --> 00:13:13,084
Uh-huh.

330
00:13:13,126 --> 00:13:16,170
Yeah, I-I have a knack
for impressions.

331
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:17,796
Well, maybe
after we get reacquainted

332
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:19,424
uh, you could do me.

333
00:13:19,466 --> 00:13:21,635
Yeah... No!

334
00:13:30,477 --> 00:13:31,728
Cassie...

335
00:13:31,770 --> 00:13:34,105
how you...
how you doing on that...

336
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:37,066
hot dog?

337
00:13:37,108 --> 00:13:39,319
I'm all done.

338
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,571
Thank God.

339
00:13:43,573 --> 00:13:45,824
I guess the last time
we really hung out

340
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:47,034
was when our parents

341
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,536
rented that beach house
together.

342
00:13:48,578 --> 00:13:50,246
Oh, right, right...

343
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:53,625
Oh, remember the time I, uh, I
pinned you down and tickled you

344
00:13:53,667 --> 00:13:54,875
until you cried?

345
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:59,130
We're probably too old
to do that now.

346
00:13:59,172 --> 00:14:03,968
I'll always remember that summer
because it's when I got

347
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,679
all these freckles.

348
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:06,971
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

349
00:14:07,013 --> 00:14:08,889
And-and...

350
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:11,476
I'll always remember that summer

351
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:15,647
because that's when
I realized that we are related.

352
00:14:15,689 --> 00:14:17,816
It took you that long
to figure it out, huh?

353
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,984
Um... I'm a little slow.

354
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:24,364
Just as our children would be.

355
00:14:31,037 --> 00:14:32,330
Hi.

356
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:33,331
How are you?

357
00:14:33,373 --> 00:14:34,332
Good.

358
00:14:34,374 --> 00:14:36,000
Hi, thanks for coming.

359
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:37,001
Thank you.

360
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:38,002
No? All right.

361
00:14:38,044 --> 00:14:39,170
Oh, so nice to see you.

362
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:41,047
Do you want-- Okay.

363
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:42,089
Hey, Rach.

364
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,216
Yeah?

365
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:45,051
Who the hell are
all these people?

366
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:46,427
Well, I don't know.

367
00:14:46,469 --> 00:14:48,137
I called all the people
in Monica's phone book

368
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:50,223
and these are the only ones
that could show up

369
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:51,224
on 24 hours notice.

370
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,266
Huh.

371
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,518
You know, there's
another word

372
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,602
for people like that.

373
00:14:54,644 --> 00:14:55,603
Losers.

374
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:58,398
Hi. I'm Rachel.

375
00:14:58,439 --> 00:14:59,524
This is Phoebe.

376
00:14:59,566 --> 00:15:00,608
I'm the Maid of Honor.

377
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:01,860
How do you know Monica?

378
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,486
I was her accountant
four years ago.

379
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:04,738
Oh.
Mmm.

380
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:06,280
I'm very interested
to find out

381
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:07,782
who's been doing her taxes

382
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:08,949
the last four years.

383
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:11,994
That's great.

384
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,540
So, what time is Monica
supposed to get here?

385
00:15:15,582 --> 00:15:17,834
I don't know.
I don't know.

386
00:15:17,876 --> 00:15:20,253
Excuse us for sec.

387
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:24,215
You didn't tell her
to come?

388
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:25,717
You were supposed
to tell her.

389
00:15:25,759 --> 00:15:26,760
No, I wasn't.

390
00:15:26,801 --> 00:15:27,886
You were supposed
to tell her.

391
00:15:27,926 --> 00:15:29,262
I was supposed
to bring the cake.

392
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,013
Fine. I'll go call her.

393
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:33,600
Yes, and please tell her
to bring a cake.

394
00:15:39,773 --> 00:15:42,066
Okay, we have
a lot of options here.

395
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:44,778
A number of prototypes
for you to try on.

396
00:15:44,819 --> 00:15:46,738
Wow, those look great.

397
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:47,822
Yeah.

398
00:15:47,864 --> 00:15:49,783
Okay, this one's
a mushroom cap.

399
00:15:49,824 --> 00:15:51,910
Uh, this one is
made of bologna.

400
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:53,411
And-and the toothpicks?

401
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:54,913
Oh, just until
the glue dries.

402
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:56,456
Thank God.

403
00:15:56,497 --> 00:16:00,794
Now these are
more realistic,
but perishable.

404
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:01,795
Oh.
Okay?

405
00:16:01,836 --> 00:16:02,879
Over here, we have

406
00:16:02,921 --> 00:16:04,297
pink suede, which is nice

407
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:05,590
but, um, if it gets wet

408
00:16:05,632 --> 00:16:07,550
then, you know, it's
going to shrink.

409
00:16:07,592 --> 00:16:10,511
Yeah, maybe we just
take that one away.

410
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:13,431
I also did a little
something in fur

411
00:16:13,473 --> 00:16:16,225
but, um, that's
really just for me.

412
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:17,351
Okay, um...

413
00:16:18,812 --> 00:16:20,104
So why don't you
go into your room

414
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:21,522
and try these on
and we'll see--

415
00:16:21,564 --> 00:16:23,399
we'll get a better idea
of what's going to work.

416
00:16:23,441 --> 00:16:25,276
Thanks.
You are such a good friend

417
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:27,153
and this is so weird.

418
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:34,786
Ow!

419
00:16:34,828 --> 00:16:35,787
Toothpick?

420
00:16:35,829 --> 00:16:38,539
Yeah.

421
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:40,124
What are you trying on now?

422
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:41,208
The fruit roll-up.

423
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,209
And?

424
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,461
Delicious.

425
00:16:43,503 --> 00:16:45,421
Joey...

426
00:16:45,463 --> 00:16:46,965
Wait a minute.
Wait a minute.

427
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:49,467
We have a winner.

428
00:16:49,509 --> 00:16:51,010
What? Which one?

429
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:53,053
The Silly Putty.

430
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:55,807
Not so silly anymore.

431
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:07,819
She's your cousin.

432
00:17:07,861 --> 00:17:10,822
She's your cousin.

433
00:17:10,864 --> 00:17:14,492
If she knew what was
going on in your head

434
00:17:14,534 --> 00:17:16,870
she'd think
you were sick.

435
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:24,293
Or would she?

436
00:17:24,335 --> 00:17:26,671
Let's back up for a second.

437
00:17:26,713 --> 00:17:31,551
She was the one who suggested
opening a bottle of wine.

438
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:34,220
She was the one
who turned down the lights.

439
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:36,472
She was the one
that wanted to rent

440
00:17:36,514 --> 00:17:41,811
Logan's Run,
the sexiest movie ever.

441
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:47,692
Oh, I know that look.

442
00:17:47,734 --> 00:17:50,194
Forget it. I want it.

443
00:17:50,236 --> 00:17:51,821
She wants it.

444
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:53,573
I'm going in.

445
00:18:00,997 --> 00:18:02,957
( gasps )

446
00:18:02,999 --> 00:18:05,084
What the hell
are you doing?

447
00:18:06,586 --> 00:18:08,462
Say something clever.

448
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,217
Okay, doesn't
have to be clever.

449
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:14,844
Just has to be words.

450
00:18:14,886 --> 00:18:18,305
Say some words.

451
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:21,100
Any words will do.

452
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:24,687
Oh, my God.

453
00:18:24,729 --> 00:18:32,152
This is the longest that anyone
has not... talked... ever.

454
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:34,906
There is nothing you could say
to make this worse

455
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:38,117
so just say something!

456
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:43,456
I-I-I haven't had sex
in a very long time.

457
00:18:47,085 --> 00:18:49,712
Yeah, you really shouldn't have
said anything.

458
00:18:52,799 --> 00:18:54,968
Phoebe, Rachel... it's Monica.

459
00:18:55,009 --> 00:18:58,262
I wonder what you could possibly
need me for

460
00:18:58,304 --> 00:18:59,889
in such short notice.

461
00:19:03,017 --> 00:19:04,351
Oh.

462
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:07,271
Oh, Monica, we
are so sorry.

463
00:19:07,313 --> 00:19:09,065
For what?

464
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:12,359
Well, first, for forgetting
to throw you a bridal shower.

465
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:15,029
And then, for forgetting
to invite you to it.

466
00:19:16,823 --> 00:19:18,908
You already had it?

467
00:19:18,950 --> 00:19:21,452
Yeah, well, we called
everyone in your phone book

468
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:22,787
and a bunch of people came

469
00:19:22,829 --> 00:19:24,789
but it took us so long
to get you here

470
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:26,040
that they had to leave.

471
00:19:26,082 --> 00:19:27,834
RACHEL:
Yeah, we wanted
to throw you

472
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:30,336
a big surprise
and a great shower

473
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:33,131
and... and now you
don't have either.

474
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,882
We ruined everything.

475
00:19:34,924 --> 00:19:36,425
Well, no, wait a minute.

476
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:37,760
That's not true.

477
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:39,971
No, what you did,
that was really sweet.

478
00:19:40,013 --> 00:19:41,973
And it kind of works out
for the best.

479
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:44,183
What do you mean?

480
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:46,144
Well, now I get to spend
my shower

481
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,228
with the only people
I really love.

482
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,981
I mean, I get all those presents

483
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:52,316
without having to talk
to a bunch of people

484
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:53,359
I don't even like.

485
00:19:59,032 --> 00:20:01,909
S-surprise.
Surprise, Monica.

486
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,500
And what's cool is,
the character

487
00:20:09,542 --> 00:20:10,918
is from Naples, right?

488
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,919
Yeah.

489
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:14,088
My whole family's from Naples.

490
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:15,548
Oh, that's great.

491
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:20,720
Okay, well, I've heard
everything I need to hear...

492
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:24,015
we just need to,
uh... Leslie?

493
00:20:24,057 --> 00:20:26,184
Uh, Joey, this is
the awkward part.

494
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:27,309
Oh, hey, right.

495
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:28,352
Not a problem.

496
00:20:28,394 --> 00:20:29,854
I totally understand.

497
00:20:29,896 --> 00:20:31,522
You need to, you know

498
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:35,275
make sure I don't have any
horrible scars or tattoos.

499
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:36,610
Don't you worry

500
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,696
I have nothing to hide.

501
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:42,533
So, there you go.

502
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:43,951
That's me.

503
00:20:43,993 --> 00:20:46,871
100% natural.

504
00:20:46,913 --> 00:20:49,540
( putty bounces and rolls )

505
00:21:01,719 --> 00:21:05,723
I tell you that has never
happened before.

506
00:21:11,938 --> 00:21:14,065
Cassie, are you finding
everything okay in there?

507
00:21:14,107 --> 00:21:15,274
Yeah. Thank you
so much

508
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:16,609
for letting me
stay here.

509
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,736
Oh, it's no problem.
I've...

510
00:21:24,033 --> 00:21:28,412
BARRY WHITE:
♪ It feels so good ♪

511
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,623
♪ You lying here next to me ♪

512
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:37,255
♪ Oh, what a groove... ♪

513
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:39,090
( music stops )
What?

514
00:21:39,132 --> 00:21:40,841
Say something.

515
00:21:40,883 --> 00:21:42,468
Say anything.

516
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:44,511
Ask her out,
she's not your cousin.

